    "skills_preload_behaviour": {
      "status": "resolved",
      "result": "missing skill = silent no-op; real skill = genuine preload",
      "detail": "Nonexistent skill in agent frontmatter does not fail the spawn and emits no warning. A declared skill that exists IS preloaded into agent context (marker token present with zero tool uses). Hence 4.0.0 needed no hotfix, and the removal needed a regression test. Also measured: Agent({team_name}) teammates do NOT receive frontmatter preloads, which is why injection writes a managed body block as well."
    }
